<title>USA: U.S. interest rates mostly higher in latest week.</title>
<headline>U.S. interest rates mostly higher in latest week.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve announced average interest rates for the week ended April 18, compared with the April 11 week, as follows:</p>
<p>   Federal funds rate.................5.48 vs 5.37</p>
<p>   3-month Treasury bills.............5.16 vs 5.14</p>
<p>   3-month commercial paper...........5.71 vs 5.69</p>
<p>   3-month bankers acceptances........5.62 vs 5.62</p>
<p>   3-month CDs........................5.72 vs 5.70</p>
<p>   3-month Eurodollar.................5.70 vs 5.69</p>
<p>   30-year Government bond............7.10 vs 7.12</p>
</text>
